    "durationMs": 523820,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and fully verified against the requirements.\n\n**What I built:**\n- **`src/main.rs`** — axum 0.8.4 app with sqlx (PostgreSQL, runtime queries + embedded `sqlx::migrate!`): `POST /links` (201, generated 8-char codes, 409 on duplicate custom code), `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `items`/`total`), `GET /links/{code}` (404 on unknown), `GET /r/{code}` (302 + atomic `UPDATE … clicks = clicks + 1 RETURNING url`). All rejections — malformed JSON, missing/invalid url, invalid code — return 422 with an `error` field. URLs are stored and returned byte-for-byte unchanged; `DATABASE_URL` is read from the environment (with a bounded retry while the DB starts).\n- **`migrations/0001_create_links.sql`** — `links` table with unique `code`, `clicks`, `BIGSERIAL id` for stable ordering; migrations apply at startup before serving.\n- **`start.sh`** (executable) — applies migrations then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n- **`README.md`** — endpoint docs and server startup instructions.\n\n**Verification:** warning-free release build; 41/41 HTTP checks passed (status codes, exact bodies, duplicate 409, six invalid-url cases, code length/charset bounds, missing url, malformed JSON, Location header, click counting); restart test confirmed clicks (3 → 3 after restart → 4 after next redirect) and all links persist. The test server is stopped and port 8000 is free."
